     1,
     "<div dir=\"auto\">Hi Sonja and welcome,<div dir=\"auto\">You can use manually created folders,. no problem.</div>When providing your own path, don&#39;t use the system.file() function. It is only for the example. Just give the path as a character string. Copy paste the path from the file explorer is fine (note that on windows one has to exchange the slashes, but not on Linux &amp; Mac).<div dir=\"auto\">Spaces in path names are allowed, but generally better avoided… at least for data analysis purposes.</div><div dir=\"auto\"><br></div><div dir=\"auto\">For the other issues I need to know the exact error messages and the code you used.</div><div dir=\"auto\"><br></div><div dir=\"auto\">Thank you,</div><div dir=\"auto\">Jürgen </div><div dir=\"auto\"><div dir=\"auto\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\" dir=\"auto\"></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"auto\"><div dir=\"auto\"><div dir=\"auto\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\" dir=\"auto\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thu, Jun 29, 2023, 17:49 Sonja Heiliger &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">sonja.he...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
